{"name":"Cumin","hex":"#a58459","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cumin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The flowering plant Cuminum cyminum, in the family Apiaceae.","Its aromatic long seed, used as a spice, notably in Indian, Middle Eastern, and Mexican cookery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cumin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cumin","blocks":[{"text":"Cumin is a flowering plant in the family Apiaceae, native to the Irano-Turanian Region. Its seeds – each one contained within a fruit, which is dried – are used in the cuisines of many cultures in both whole and ground form. Although cumin is used in traditional medicine, there is no high-quality evidence that it is safe or effective as a therapeutic agent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Cuminum_cyminum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-198.jpg/330px-Cuminum_cyminum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-198.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumin"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Sa_cumin.jpg/500px-Sa_cumin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Sa_cumin.jpg/1280px-Sa_cumin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Sa_cumin.jpg/500px-Sa_cumin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cumin seeds, about 5 mm long.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASa_cumin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Black_Cumin.jpg/500px-Black_Cumin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Black_Cumin.jpg/1280px-Black_Cumin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip